gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda x}-5\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda x}+\\frac{25}{4}{e}^{\\lambda x} & =0 \\\\ {e}^{\\lambda x}({\\lambda }^{2}-5\\lambda +\\frac{25}{4}) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe auxiliary equation is therefore\n\n$$\n{\\lambda }^{2}-5\\lambda +\\frac{25}{4}=0.\n$$\n\nFactoring the auxiliary equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\lambda -\\frac{5}{2})(\\lambda -\\frac{5}{2}) & =0 \\\\ {(\\lambda -\\frac{5}{2})}^{2} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\lambda =\\frac{5}{2}$ is a repeated root.\n\nSo the general solution to the differential equation is\n\n$$\ny=A{e}^{5x/2}+Bx{e}^{5x/2}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-7796/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bebe4460-e57e-546f-99c8-81192aafc1ec"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-7796"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-90958/selection/521e01edb667d791c38945a78da4917e03a7ce003d3b29a80d8f55f8ebf4682c" :answer/id #uuid "9f2fad6b-8a46-5ad0-a43e-abc1bf01ba13" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=A{e}^{14x}+Bx{e}^{14x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-90958/selection/59bc0bd3a61fdbacaeac18de4c435b085e4990a6ad67e87048d35deaef870af4" :answer/id #uuid "e46a9e0d-46a9-57e7-887c-c8b8a2d180ba" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=A{e}^{7x}+B{e}^{-7x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-90958/selection/0d1368ec6b650731824f3b37a2ad5e0824674db83cc47f60720e4dbca6817ac0" :answer/id #uuid "8eebe685-4a07-5834-a522-c34f90d5e144" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=A{e}^{7x}+Bx{e}^{7x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-90958/selection/dc4bedef546c93eafd11afc08db13c156f077a5c99f4281a7ca15d27fab4ead5" :answer/id #uuid "ee747339-5773-5dbe-82df-92b150112545" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=A{e}^{-7x}+Bx{e}^{-7x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-90958/selection/79ebd914793ca7d6e6ab2993d0bb595067f3f43728897