to the differential equation is\n\n$$\ny=A{e}^{7x}+Bx{e}^{7x}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-90958/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bebe4460-e57e-546f-99c8-81192aafc1ec"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-90958"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-90964/selection/cde2cedb8f2e21a50c5ed7839e8c8f29d67a9ad6eedfbc4cf25e8111d9ed5eea" :answer/id #uuid "ac6e7f21-4497-5431-82cd-4bde85e0f2c1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3{e}^{-3x/2}+x{e}^{-3x/2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-90964/selection/463d379f8a1b2cc0851c7d24e0890e5c4486c832a06dec8d80323366dfdbfaeb" :answer/id #uuid "01212f94-c28e-551b-b234-15745b2af8a8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8{e}^{-3x/2}-3x{e}^{-3x/2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-90964/selection/8650f885cd9f32932fc86ae9dd9c8fe06a5eea1c07785b437767e6f8f7f9e1f1" :answer/id #uuid "b724f176-6ecf-5109-abbc-4ede71c24472" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{-3x/2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-90964/selection/77681a941b300019ab1ab65131d30b6bf9f50e98195dfd5cf130dfeb77522df8" :answer/id #uuid "9c9f780d-09e0-50fb-953d-191a31331823" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x{e}^{-3x/2}-3{x}^{2}{e}^{-3x/2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-90964/selection/6a48d064bb9c3f2ce53272cbc3e78dbf183ba7ee6a3223dfcb2fc2003e109e32" :answer/id #uuid "c53afb34-e362-5f7d-a28c-0e2fe9e7ba74" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2x{e}^{-3x/2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-90964/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "d2d588e1-f81d-529c-8085-6d681afa8b44" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-90964/selection/77681a941b300019ab1ab65131d30b6bf9f50e98195dfd5cf130dfeb77522df8" :answer-field/choices ["q-90964/selection/cde2cedb8f2e21a50c5ed7839e8c8f29d67a9ad6eedfbc4cf25e8111d9ed5eea" "q-90964/selection/463d379f8a1b2cc0851c7d24e0890e5c4486c832a06dec8d80323366dfdbfaeb" "q-90964/selection/8650f885cd9f32932fc86ae9dd9c8fe06a5eea1c07785b437767e6f8f7f9e1f1" "q-90964/selection/77681a941b300019ab1ab65131d30b6bf9f50e98195dfd5cf130dfeb77522df8" "q-90964/selection/6a48d064bb9c3f2ce53272cbc3e78dbf183ba7ee6a3223dfcb2fc2003e109e32"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-90964" :question/id #uuid "da67980d-2aed-51d8-92a4-0f5a69c4f7f8" :question/math-academy-id "q-90964" :question/problem "Given the equation ${y}^{″}+3{y}^{′}+\\frac{9}{4}y=0$ for $y=y(x),$ which of the following is **not** a solution to this equation?" :question/worked-solution "Assuming $y={e}^{\\lambda x}$ and differentiating $y$ with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda x},\\,{y}^{″}={\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda x}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda x}+3\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda x}+\\frac{9}{4}{e}^{\\lambda x} & =0 \\\\ {e}^{\\lambda x}({\\lambda }^{2}+3\\lambda +\\frac{9}{4}) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe auxiliary equation is therefore\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}+3\\lambda +\\frac{9}{4} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFactoring the auxiliary equation results in\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(\\lambda +\\frac{3}{2})}^{2} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand so $\\lambda =-\\frac{3}{2}$ is a repeated root of the auxiliary equation.\n\nTherefore, any linear combination of the functions ${e}^{-3x/2}$ and $x{e}^{-3x/2}$ is a solution to the original differential equation. \n\nAmong the given options, only $x{e}^{-3x/2}-3{x}^{2}{e}^{-3x/2}$ is not a solution." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-90964/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b4ad20bb-c6a4-5390-a11a-e5277cfd1667"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-90964"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-90966/selection/9a4df386f60e3f75f7321e868bbf138156f7693043a8160e407710974d54f1cb" :answer/id #uuid "9c7c1f4c-2a0e-583f-80ca-190f6f9ad206" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{8x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-90966/selection/7df430eeefe8afefdd7ff37a1660876167160786d55bdc2117acd89d74560de6" :answer/id #uuid "66c6c3de-1dce-5f5d-bfec-3dca532696ae" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{8x}-x{e}^{8x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-90966/selection/ff3f0275709f4add2e496c6e151e7831209c8e188a56f259aa0f8279dacc808d" :answer/id #uuid "e3201b11-407a-50f7-8db9-8d155d0dfa03" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2x{e}^{8x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-90966/selection/a26cd8e6aba0cbe00ccf955643db26cb904ecfe23db5367ad0cf1d758295255e" :answer/id #uuid "f02dd178-08d6-5d24-841b-2fed48d0c76a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{2}{e}^{8x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-90966/selection/15c4b69074a671f395a006e60a636692858fefe7751c4e47e4b6043577186314" :answer/id #uuid "0c1c1090-259e-5daa-9901-295e9ecedbcb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3{e}^{8x}+2x{e}^{8x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-90966/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "fe7af11e-c46b-5752-8048-022210ff7b9e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-90966/selection/a26cd8e6aba0cbe00ccf955643db26cb904ecfe23db5367ad0cf1d758295255e" :answer-field/choices ["q-90966/selection/9a4df386f60e3f75f7321e868bbf138156f7693043a8160e407710974d54f1cb" "q-90966/selection/7df430eeefe8afefdd7ff37a1660876167160786d55bdc2117acd89d74560de6" "q-90966/selection/ff3f0275709f4add2e496c6e151e7831209c8e188a56f259aa0f8279dacc808d" "q-90966/selection/a26cd8e6aba0cbe00ccf955643db26cb904ecfe23db5367ad0cf1d758295255e" "q-90966/selection/15c4b69074a671f395a006e60a636692858fefe7751c4e47e4b6043577186314"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-90966" :question/id #uuid "55caafa4-33d6-5292-85be-7e2f3497a749" :question/math-academy-id "q-90966" :question/problem "Given the equation ${y}^{″}-16{y}^{′}+64y=0$ for $y=y(x),$ which of the following is **not** a solution to this equation?" :question/worked-solution "Assuming $y={e}^{\\lambda x}$ and differentiating $y$ with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda x},\\,{y}^{″}={\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda x}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda x}-16\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda x}+64{e}^{\\lambda x} & =0 \\\\ {e}^{\\lambda x}({\\lambda }^{2}-16\\lambda +64) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe auxiliary equation is therefore\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}-16\\lambda +64 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFactoring the auxiliary equation results in\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(\\lambda -8)}^{2} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand so $\\lambda =8$ is a repeated root of the auxiliary equation.\n\nTherefore, any linear combination of the functions ${e}^{8x}$ and $x{e}^{8x}$ is a solution to the original differential equation. \n\nAmong the given options, only ${x}^{2}{e}^{8x}$ is not a solution." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-90966/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b4ad20bb-c6a4-5390-a11a-e5277cfd1667"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-90966"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
